# Nothing in this file is required.
#
# Nextup can be set up entirely from its own pages: run it, open it, and it
# asks for a Jellyfin administrator sign-in and then for whichever acquisition
# tools you run, testing each one and listing its quality profiles for you.
# This file is the alternative, for a deployment you would rather describe than
# click through.
#
# Anything set here WINS over the pages. A value in a compose file is a
# statement about a deployment, so the Backends page shows it, says it is held
# in the environment, and does not offer to change it.
#
# `docker compose exec nextup python -m app.doctor` reads whichever is in
# effect and says, by name, what is missing and what is not answering.

# --- Jellyfin ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Set these only to skip the setup page. JELLYFIN_TOKEN is an API key from
# Dashboard -> API Keys; leave it out and the setup page obtains one for itself
# from an administrator sign-in.
#JELLYFIN_TOKEN=
# Where Jellyfin is, from inside the container. Never `localhost`: inside a
# container that is the container itself.
#JELLYFIN_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8096

# Which port to publish the web pages on.
#NEXTUP_PORT=8099

# --- Films: Radarr -----------------------------------------------------------
#RADARR_URL=http://radarr:7878
#RADARR_API_KEY=
# No default, deliberately: which profile a household wants is a real choice
# about disk and bandwidth. The Backends page lists Radarr's own profiles to
# pick from, which is easier than finding this number.
#RADARR_QUALITY_PROFILE_ID=
# Only needed when Radarr has more than one root folder.
#RADARR_ROOT_FOLDER=

# --- Television: Sonarr ------------------------------------------------------
#SONARR_URL=http://sonarr:8989
#SONARR_API_KEY=
#SONARR_QUALITY_PROFILE_ID=
#SONARR_ROOT_FOLDER=
# Sonarr's own vocabulary: all, firstSeason, future, missing, existing, none.
# `all` because somebody asking for a series they do not have means the series.
#SONARR_MONITOR=all

# --- Audiobooks: Listenarr ---------------------------------------------------
#LISTENARR_URL=http://listenarr:4545
#LISTENARR_QUALITY_PROFILE_ID=1
# Marketplaces to consult, in order. A list because a library can span two: the
# same book is on one store and not the other often enough that a single region
# answers with an empty product, and an empty product is what fills a request
# with the wrong book.
#AUDIBLE_REGIONS=ca,us

# --- Music: buskarr ----------------------------------------------------------
#BUSKARR_URL=http://buskarr:8000
#BUSKARR_API_KEY=

# --- Allowances --------------------------------------------------------------
# Per account per rolling day, per medium. Separate counters because the media
# are not the same size: a film is one file, a series is a season or ten, and
# one artist can resolve to hundreds of tracks. Jellyfin administrators are
# uncapped.
#MOVIE_DAILY_CAP=3
#SERIES_DAILY_CAP=1
#MUSIC_DAILY_CAP=3
#BOOK_DAILY_CAP=3

# --- Libraries ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Only set these to narrow things down. Unset, each medium uses every Jellyfin
# view of the matching collection type, which is right on almost every server.
#MOVIE_LIBRARY_IDS=
#SERIES_LIBRARY_IDS=
#MUSIC_LIBRARY_IDS=
#BOOK_LIBRARY_IDS=

# --- The book shelf's reading list in Jellyfin -------------------------------
# The book recommendations are kept as a reading list per account, so they can
# be read by any Jellyfin client rather than only by one that speaks this API.
# Jellyfin stores it as a playlist item -- that is what it calls any ordered
# list -- so that is where to look for it on the server. The names below are
# what a person sees, and a list of books should not be called a playlist to
# them.
#PLAYLIST_NAME=Next Read
# One account's list keeps that name unsuffixed; everybody else's is
# "Next Read — <their name>". Set this to whichever account was already using
# the bare name, or leave it unset on a fresh install where nobody was.
#PLAYLIST_OWNER=
# How often the shelves, and so the reading list, are refreshed for accounts
# that already have one. Zero turns the pass off and leaves the list written
# only when something asks for a shelf.
#BOOK_UPKEEP_HOURS=6

# --- Discovery ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Where native clients reach this service at the Jellyfin origin, e.g.
# https://jellyfin.example.com/nextup. Only used to check that route is really
# there: leaving that proxy rule out is the easiest half of a deployment to
# forget and the only one with no symptom at all. Warn-only, never a health
# failure. Unnecessary if you only use the web pages.
#
# Comma-separated if you serve more than one prefix -- an upgrade from the
# separate audiobook service also answers .../nextread, and that route fails
# just as silently.
#PUBLIC_URL=

# --- If a sign-in proxy is in front of the pages -----------------------------
# The header it forwards a username in. Ignore this if you are not running one.
#AUTH_USER_HEADER=X-Auth-Request-Preferred-Username
# A single account to assume when no proxy header and no session cookie is
# present. Leave empty on anything more than one person can reach.
#JELLYFIN_USER=

#LOG_LEVEL=INFO
